<launch>
  <!-- Grasp-and-deliver sequencing.

         /orchestrator/run_navigate_report   orchestrator/RunRoute
         /orchestrator/run_grasp             orchestrator/RunRoute
         /orchestrator/run_deliver           orchestrator/RunRoute
         /orchestrator/run_deliver_task      orchestrator/RunRoute  <- full task
         /orchestrator/run_fetch_deliver     orchestrator/RunRoute  <- spoken task
         /orchestrator/run_auto_release      orchestrator/RunRoute
         /orchestrator/status                std_msgs/String (latched)

       DRY RUN BY DEFAULT. With enable_motion:=false (the default) no robot
       service client is constructed at all, every step is traversed and
       nothing moves, so a route can be rehearsed with the robot powered off:

         rosservice call /orchestrator/run_navigate_report "{target: table}"

       A real run needs enable_motion:=true AND a clean preflight. One blocker
       means zero steps and zero motion, with the full list returned.

       The grasp route is permanently NOT_READY for a real run: it needs the
       unresolved perception to arm_planning frame contract.

       fetch_deliver is the route the voice command runs ("go to the desk,
       pick up a can, go to the chair, and pass me"): standing waypoints,
       perception, arm_grasp and handover_node: the modules that have run
       on this robot. target / destination are standing waypoint names of
       map_name (slam/maps/<map_name>/standing_waypoints.yaml):

         rosservice call /orchestrator/run_fetch_deliver \
           "{target: table_01, destination: chair_01, label: bottle}"
  -->
  <arg name="config" default="$(find orchestrator)/config/orchestrator.yaml"/>
  <arg name="enable_motion" default="false"/>
  <arg name="side" default="right"/>
  <!-- Map whose standing waypoints fetch_deliver resolves against. Pass the
       same map_name as the localization launch. -->
  <arg name="map_name" default="current"/>

  <node pkg="orchestrator" type="orchestrator_node.py" name="orchestrator" output="screen">
    <rosparam command="load" file="$(arg config)"/>
    <param name="enable_motion" type="bool" value="$(arg enable_motion)"/>
    <param name="side" value="$(arg side)"/>
    <param name="map_name" value="$(arg map_name)"/>
  </node>
</launch>
